"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2719,"###
 Narrated to us by Abu Bishr al-Wasiti, who said: Narrated to us by Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas, ""The Ramal (brisk walking with shoulders heaving) is done for three circuits around the House, and four circuits are done walking normally. Indeed, your people claim that this is a Sunnah."" He replied, ""They have spoken the truth, and they have spoken a lie."" He continued,"
2720,"Narrated to us Nasr ibn Marzuq: narrated to us Asad: informed us Hammad ibn Salamah: from Ayyub: from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: from Ibn 'Abbas (RA) that the Quraysh said, ""Indeed, Muhammad (ﷺ) and his Companions have been weakened by the fever of Yathrib (Madinah)."" So when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in the year in which he arrived, he said to his Companions, ""Perform *ramal* (fast walking with short steps) around the House three times so that the polytheists may see your strength."" So when they performed *ramal*, the Quraysh said, ""They have not been weakened by the fever.""

**CHAPTER:**"
